From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 20:22:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add common ToolStrip configuration members

Add the frequently-referenced ToolStrip surface that was missing - AllowItemReorder,
AllowMerge, CanOverflow, ShowItemToolTips, Stretch, IsDropDown (virtual, overridden
true by ToolStripDropDown), Orientation, TextDirection, DefaultDropDownDirection,
ImageList, Renderer (never null, defaults to ToolStripProfessionalRenderer) and
OverflowButton. Because they live on the base, they propagate to the whole cluster
(MenuStrip, StatusStrip, ContextMenuStrip, the drop-downs, BindingNavigator).

They compile and round-trip with WinForms defaults; the GTK substrate does not
fully honour the layout/rendering they name, but ported source that reads or sets
them works. Covered by ToolStripMembersFunctionalTests. Full Forms suite green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
